==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-brush off.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{&lit|en|brush|off}} To [[remove]] something with a [[brush]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[disregard]] (something), to [[dismiss]] or [[ignore]] (someone), as unimportant.
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XVIII|passage=Again I begged her to keep an eye on her blood pressure and not get so worked up, and once more she '''brushed me off''', this time with a curt request that I would go and boil my head.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} To [[depart]] with a sweeping motion.
#* {{RQ:Goldsmith Venison|page=8|passage=Thus, ſeizing his hat, he '''bruſh'd''' off like the vvind, / And the Porter and Eatables follovv'd behind.}}

